# A-01 — Hello World REST API
## Terminal Commands & Quick Reference

**Project location:**
`C:\Users\rkrev\Downloads\New folder\A01-Hello-World-API`

### 1. Start the project

Open PowerShell and execute these commands in order:

**Step 1 — Navigate to the project folder**
```powershell
cd "C:\Users\rkrev\Downloads\New folder\A01-Hello-World-API"
```

**Step 2 — Activate virtual environment**
```powershell
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

**Step 3 — Start FastAPI**
```powershell
python -m uvicorn main:app --reload
```

Your server should display:
```text
Uvicorn running on http://127.0.0.1:8000
Application startup complete.
```

### 2. Open the API in your browser

| URL | Purpose |
|---|---|
| http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | API response |
| http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs | Swagger interactive documentation |
| http://127.0.0.1:8000/openapi.json | OpenAPI specification |

### 3. Stop the server

Press:
```text
Ctrl + C
```

This stops the running Uvicorn server.

### 4. Deactivate virtual environment

After stopping the server:
```powershell
deactivate
```

This exits the project's Python virtual environment.

### 5. Install dependencies

If setting up the project on a new machine or recreating the virtual environment:

```powershell
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 6. Git and GitHub commands

Run these inside the project folder.

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `git status` | Check changed and untracked files |
| `git add .` | Stage project changes |
| `git add main.py` | Stage one specific file |
| `git commit -m "message"` | Save a local commit |
| `git push` | Upload commits to GitHub |
| `git pull` | Download and integrate remote changes |
| `git log --oneline` | View commit history |
| `git remote -v` | Check connected GitHub repository |

**First-time Git setup** (already done for this project):
```powershell
git init
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/rkrevanth295-arch/Hello-World-REST-API-.git
```

### 7. Important project files

```text
A01-Hello-World-API/
│
├── main.py             # FastAPI application
├── requirements.txt    # Python dependencies
├── README.md           # Project documentation
├── .gitignore          # Files Git should ignore
├── venv/               # Python virtual environment
└── __pycache__/        # Automatically generated Python cache
```

### 8. Troubleshooting

| Problem | Solution |
|---|---|
| `Could not import module main` | Check that you're inside the project folder and `main.py` exists |
| `No module named fastapi` | Activate venv and install requirements |
| `uvicorn is not recognized` | Use `python -m uvicorn main:app --reload` |
| Port 8000 already in use | Stop the other server or use `--port 8001` |
| PowerShell blocks activation | Run `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass` and activate again |
| Git push rejected | Run `git pull` first and resolve any conflicts |

**Remember:**

- `venv` keeps project dependencies isolated.
- `Uvicorn` runs the FastAPI server.
- `--reload` automatically restarts the server when you change Python code.
- `Ctrl + C` stops the server.
- `deactivate` exits the virtual environment.
- `git push` uploads your committed changes to GitHub.

**GitHub repository:** https://github.com/rkrevanth295-arch/Hello-World-REST-API-
